IMPORT prelude

-- Northwest Territories Income Tax Act, R.S.N.W.T. 1988, c.I-1 -- the tax of an individual resident in the Northwest
-- Territories on the last day of the year, and the two benefits the Act pays through the tax system:
--   who pays (s 2(1)(a)); the tax on the amount taxable (s 2.11(2), (4), (5)) and how the thresholds are indexed
--   (s 2.11(6), (7)); the main non-refundable credits (ss 2.14, 2.15, 2.16, 2.2, 2.21, 2.22, 2.24(1), 2.26, 2.29 and the
--   federal provisions applied by ss 2.25, 2.28); the dividend deduction (s 2.32); the NWT Child Benefit (ss 3.1, 3.2,
--   with the amounts and thresholds of Income Tax Regulations s 1.1); and the Cost of Living Offset (s 3.5, with the
--   zone amounts of Income Tax Regulations s 1.2).
--
-- SEAT: the individual taxpayer resident in the Northwest Territories, and the parent who claims the NWT Child Benefit.
-- "How much territorial tax do I pay? What credits do I get? How much NWT Child Benefit and Cost of Living Offset do I
-- get?" The Commissioner and the federal Minister appear only as what they must or may do for that person.
--
-- Edition: the office consolidation of the Act dated 2023-11-23 (last amendment SNWT 2023, c.30), and of the Income Tax
-- Regulations, R.R.N.W.T. 1990, c.I-1, dated 2025-06-02 (last amendment R-038-2025), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/income-tax.a.2023-11-23.txt and
-- ../../../income-tax-regulations/registers/source-bundle/income-tax.r1.2025-06-02.txt.
-- The 2026 tier thresholds come from the Canada Revenue Agency's page "Current year tax rates and income brackets
-- (2026)", deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/cra-tax-rates-brackets-2026.txt (NOTES.md finding 1).
--
-- The tax starts from FEDERAL figures, which are inputs: taxable income, net income, the federal amounts that the NWT
-- credits take over (s 118(3) pension income, s 118.1 gifts, s 118.5 tuition, s 118.62 interest, s 118.7 premiums and
-- contributions), the federal "adjusted income" of s 122.6 for the Child Benefit. Read with the federal Income Tax Act
-- encoding in subjects/ca/income-tax-act/ (cross-folder IMPORT is not possible in the stable l4).
--
-- Every dollar amount in ss 2.14, 2.15, 2.16, 2.17, 2.18, 2.2, 2.23 and 2.24(1) is indexed each year by s 2.13. The
-- deposited texts do not state the indexed figures, so they are inputs (NOTES.md finding 2).
--
-- NOT ENCODED (answers `not covered` where a question can reach it): an individual not resident in the Territories on
-- the last day of the year (s 2(1)(b)); the apportionment for income earned outside the Territories (s 2.44); years before
-- 2005; the lump-sum and minimum-tax additions (ss 2.12, 2.43) and the split-income tax (s 2.42); the in-home care,
-- dependant and additional dependant credits (ss 2.17, 2.18, 2.19), the medical expense credit (s 2.23), the disability
-- supplement for a person under 18 (s 2.24(1)(c)(i)) and the transfers (ss 2.24(2), 2.3); the minimum tax carry-over
-- (s 2.31); the foreign tax deduction (s 3); corporations (ss 4 to 4.1); the political contribution credit (ss 5, 6); the
-- investment tax credit (s 6.1).
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written from the individual's seat with the 2026-10-18 defaults. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Northwest Territories Income Tax Act -- the tax of a resident individual`

§§ `Questions this encoding does not cover`

DECLARE `Why not covered` IS ONE OF
    `only an individual resident in the Northwest Territories on the last day of the year is encoded (s 2(1)(a)); s 2(1)(b) is not`
    `income earned outside the Northwest Territories brings in the apportionment of s 2.44, which is not encoded`
    `only the 2005 and later taxation years are encoded (s 2.11(2))`
    `the tier thresholds for that year are not deposited; give them, as published for the year`
    `the amount taxable cannot be negative`

GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH A TYPE
DECLARE `Answer` a IS ONE OF
    `answered`    HAS `the answer` IS AN a
    `not covered` HAS `because`    IS A `Why not covered`

§§ `Small arithmetic`

GIVEN x IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` x y MEANS IF x AT MOST y THEN x ELSE y

GIVEN x IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the greater of` x y MEANS IF x AT LEAST y THEN x ELSE y

GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`nil if negative` x MEANS `the greater of` 0 x

-- s 2.11(5), s 2.11(7), s 2.13(5): "rounded to the nearest multiple of one dollar or, if it is equidistant from two such
-- consecutive multiples, to the higher multiple."
GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`rounded to the nearest dollar` x MEANS FLOOR (x PLUS 0.5)

-- s 2.11(6)(b)(ii), s 2.13(2)(b)(ii): "rounded to the nearest one-thousandth, or, if the result obtained is equidistant
-- from two consecutive one-thousandths, to the higher one-thousandth".
GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`rounded to the nearest one-thousandth` x MEANS (FLOOR ((x TIMES 1000) PLUS 0.5)) DIVIDED BY 1000

§§ `s 2(1) -- who pays`

-- s 2(1): "An income tax shall be paid ... for each taxation year by every individual (a) who was resident in the
-- Northwest Territories on the last day of the taxation year; or (b) who, not being resident ... on the last day of the
-- taxation year, had income earned in the taxation year in the Northwest Territories". Residence is a borrowed (federal,
-- common-law) term, asked as a fact.
GIVEN `resident in the Northwest Territories on the last day of the year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `had income earned in the year in the Northwest Territories` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is liable to Northwest Territories income tax under s 2(1)` IF
        `resident in the Northwest Territories on the last day of the year`
    OR  `had income earned in the year in the Northwest Territories`

§§ `s 2.11 -- the rates, the thresholds and the tax`

-- s 2.11(2): the tier rates "for the 2005 and subsequent taxation years".
`tier one rate`   MEANS 5.9%
`tier two rate`   MEANS 8.6%
`tier three rate` MEANS 12.2%
`tier four rate`  MEANS 14.05%

-- s 2.1: "appropriate percentage" is, for 2004 and later years, the tier one rate; "highest percentage" the tier four rate.
`the appropriate percentage` MEANS `tier one rate`
`the highest percentage`     MEANS `tier four rate`

DECLARE `Thresholds` HAS
    `tier one threshold`   IS A NUMBER
    `tier two threshold`   IS A NUMBER
    `tier three threshold` IS A NUMBER

-- s 2.11(3): the 2004 thresholds, $33,245, $66,492 and $108,101; later years are indexed under s 2.11(6).
`the 2004 thresholds` MEANS `Thresholds` WITH
    `tier one threshold`   IS 33245
    `tier two threshold`   IS 66492
    `tier three threshold` IS 108101

-- The 2026 thresholds as published by the Canada Revenue Agency for the Northwest Territories ("$0 to $53,003 5.9%;
-- $53,003.01 to $106,009 8.6%; $106,009.01 to $172,346 12.2%; $172,346.01 and over 14.05%"), deposited as
-- cra-tax-rates-brackets-2026.txt. The rates it prints are the s 2.11(2) rates. NOTES.md finding 1.
`the 2026 thresholds published by the Canada Revenue Agency` MEANS `Thresholds` WITH
    `tier one threshold`   IS 53003
    `tier two threshold`   IS 106009
    `tier three threshold` IS 172346

-- s 2.11(4): the tax on the amount taxable ("taxable income or taxable income earned in Canada", s 2.11(1)), with the
-- fixed part of each tier ((4)(b)(i), (c)(i), (d)(i)) rounded under s 2.11(5).
GIVEN `amount taxable` IS A NUMBER, `thresholds` IS A `Thresholds`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the tax under s 2.11(4)` `amount taxable` `thresholds` MEANS
    IF `amount taxable` AT MOST t1
    THEN `tier one rate` TIMES `amount taxable`
    ELSE IF `amount taxable` AT MOST t2
         THEN `rounded to the nearest dollar` (`tier one rate` TIMES t1)
              PLUS (`tier two rate` TIMES (`amount taxable` MINUS t1))
         ELSE IF `amount taxable` AT MOST t3
              THEN `rounded to the nearest dollar` ((`tier one rate` TIMES t1) PLUS (`tier two rate` TIMES (t2 MINUS t1)))
                   PLUS (`tier three rate` TIMES (`amount taxable` MINUS t2))
              ELSE `rounded to the nearest dollar` ((`tier one rate` TIMES t1) PLUS (`tier two rate` TIMES (t2 MINUS t1)) PLUS (`tier three rate` TIMES (t3 MINUS t2)))
                   PLUS (`tier four rate` TIMES (`amount taxable` MINUS t3))
    WHERE
        t1 MEANS `thresholds`'s `tier one threshold`
        t2 MEANS `thresholds`'s `tier two threshold`
        t3 MEANS `thresholds`'s `tier three threshold`

-- s 2.11(6): each threshold for a year after 2004 is "the amount that would, but for subsection (7), be the amount of the
-- threshold for the preceding taxation year" plus that amount times A/B - 1, "rounded to the nearest one-thousandth", A
-- being the Consumer Price Index for the 12 months ended on 30 September of the preceding year and B that for the 12
-- months before. (7): the result is rounded to the dollar. The unrounded figure carries forward; the rounded one is used.
-- Any adjustment of the factor "in the manner that may be prescribed by federal regulations" is not encoded (NOTES.md
-- finding 3).
GIVEN `the preceding year's threshold before rounding` IS A NUMBER
      `CPI A` IS A NUMBER
      `CPI B` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the threshold before rounding under s 2.11(6)` `the preceding year's threshold before rounding` `CPI A` `CPI B` MEANS
    `the preceding year's threshold before rounding`
    PLUS (`the preceding year's threshold before rounding` TIMES `rounded to the nearest one-thousandth` ((`CPI A` DIVIDED BY `CPI B`) MINUS 1))

GIVEN `the preceding year's threshold before rounding` IS A NUMBER
      `CPI A` IS A NUMBER
      `CPI B` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the threshold under s 2.11(6) and (7)` `the preceding year's threshold before rounding` `CPI A` `CPI B` MEANS
    `rounded to the nearest dollar` (`the threshold before rounding under s 2.11(6)` `the preceding year's threshold before rounding` `CPI A` `CPI B`)

§§ `ss 2.14 to 2.16 -- the spouse, eligible dependant and single status credits`

-- ss 2.14(2)(b)(ii), 2.15(2)(b)(ii), 2.16(b)(ii): "$11,050", indexed every year after 2003 by s 2.13(3), (4). The indexed
-- figure for the year (the NWT "basic personal amount") is an input; the same indexing applies to every $11,050, so one
-- figure serves all three sections.

-- s 2.16: "Except in the case of an individual entitled to a deduction under section 2.14 or 2.15, ... A x B" with B the
-- (indexed) $11,050.
GIVEN `the indexed basic amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the single status credit under s 2.16` `the indexed basic amount` MEANS
    `the appropriate percentage` TIMES `the indexed basic amount`

-- s 2.14(2) and s 2.15(2): B is "the total of (A) $11,050, and (B) the amount determined by the formula $11,050 - C" where
-- C is the spouse's or common-law partner's income (2.14), or the dependent person's income (2.15). The text does not say
-- "if negative, nil"; the encoding reads (B) as nil when C exceeds the basic amount (NOTES.md finding 4).
GIVEN `the indexed basic amount` IS A NUMBER, `the other person's income` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 2.14 or s 2.15 credit` `the indexed basic amount` `the other person's income` MEANS
    `the appropriate percentage` TIMES (`the indexed basic amount` PLUS `nil if negative` (`the indexed basic amount` MINUS `the other person's income`))

-- s 2.14(1): married or in a common-law partnership, "supporting" the spouse or partner, and not living separate and apart
-- because of a breakdown of the relationship, at any time in the year.
-- s 2.15(1): not entitled under s 2.14; unmarried (or married and neither supporting, living with, nor supported by the
-- spouse); maintaining a self-contained domestic establishment in which the individual lives and supports a person who is
-- resident in Canada (except a child), wholly dependent on the individual, related to the individual, and under 18 or
-- dependent because of infirmity (except a parent or grandparent).
DECLARE `Household for the basic credits` IS ONE OF
    `single, with no eligible dependant`
    `supporting a spouse or common-law partner`              HAS `the spouse's income` IS A NUMBER
    `single, supporting an eligible dependant under s 2.15`  HAS `the dependant's income` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the indexed basic amount` IS A NUMBER, `household` IS A `Household for the basic credits`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the basic credits under ss 2.14 to 2.16` `the indexed basic amount` `household` MEANS
    CONSIDER `household`
    WHEN `single, with no eligible dependant` THEN `the single status credit under s 2.16` `the indexed basic amount`
    WHEN `supporting a spouse or common-law partner` i THEN `the s 2.14 or s 2.15 credit` `the indexed basic amount` i
    WHEN `single, supporting an eligible dependant under s 2.15` i THEN `the s 2.14 or s 2.15 credit` `the indexed basic amount` i

§§ `s 2.2 -- the age credit`

-- s 2.2: for an individual "who has attained the age of 65 years before the end of the year", A x (B - C): B the (indexed)
-- $5,405; C "15% of the amount, if any, by which the individual's income for the year would exceed $26,941" (indexed). Both
-- indexed figures are inputs. B - C is read as nil if negative (NOTES.md finding 4).
GIVEN `65 or over before the end of the year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my income for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the indexed age amount` IS A NUMBER
      `the indexed income threshold` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the age credit under s 2.2` `65 or over before the end of the year` `my income for the year` `the indexed age amount` `the indexed income threshold` MEANS
    IF `65 or over before the end of the year`
    THEN `the appropriate percentage` TIMES `nil if negative` (`the indexed age amount` MINUS (15% TIMES `nil if negative` (`my income for the year` MINUS `the indexed income threshold`)))
    ELSE 0

§§ `s 2.21 -- the pension credit`

-- s 2.21(1): resident in the Territories on the last day of the year; A x the lesser of $1,000 and the federal pension
-- income amount (s 118(3)(b) of the federal Act). Not indexed.
GIVEN `resident on the last day of the year` IS A BOOLEAN, `the federal s 118(3) pension income amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the pension credit under s 2.21` `resident on the last day of the year` `the federal s 118(3) pension income amount` MEANS
    IF `resident on the last day of the year`
    THEN `the appropriate percentage` TIMES `the lesser of` 1000 `the federal s 118(3) pension income amount`
    ELSE 0

§§ `s 2.22 -- the charitable donations credit`

-- s 2.22: "(A x B) + [C x (D - B)]": A the appropriate percentage, B "the lesser of $200 and the amount determined for D",
-- C the highest percentage, D the total gifts used for the federal s 118.1 deduction. Not indexed.
GIVEN `total gifts used federally` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the donations credit under s 2.22` `total gifts used federally` MEANS
    (`the appropriate percentage` TIMES b) PLUS (`the highest percentage` TIMES (`total gifts used federally` MINUS b))
    WHERE
        b MEANS `the lesser of` 200 `total gifts used federally`

§§ `s 2.24(1) -- the credit for mental or physical impairment`

-- s 2.24(1): "if the individual is entitled to a deduction under subsection 118.3(1) of the federal Act", A x (B + C): B the
-- (indexed) $8,961, an input; C "in any other case, zero". The supplement C for an individual under 18 (s 2.24(1)(c)(i))
-- is not encoded, so this function is for an individual 18 or over at the end of the year.
GIVEN `entitled to the federal disability credit under s 118.3(1)` IS A BOOLEAN, `the indexed disability amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the disability credit under s 2.24(1) for an adult` `entitled to the federal disability credit under s 118.3(1)` `the indexed disability amount` MEANS
    IF `entitled to the federal disability credit under s 118.3(1)`
    THEN `the appropriate percentage` TIMES `the indexed disability amount`
    ELSE 0

§§ `ss 2.25, 2.26, 2.28, 2.29 -- tuition, education, student loan interest, premiums and contributions`

-- s 2.25 (tuition, federal s 118.5), s 2.28 (student loan interest, federal s 118.62) and s 2.29 (EI premiums and CPP
-- contributions, federal s 118.7) apply the federal provisions with the territorial appropriate percentage; the base
-- amount is the federal one, an input.
GIVEN `the federal base amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`a credit at the appropriate percentage` `the federal base amount` MEANS
    `the appropriate percentage` TIMES `the federal base amount`

-- s 2.26(1): for a qualifying student, A x B, B the total of $400 for each month of full-time enrolment in a qualifying
-- educational program and $120 for each other month of part-time enrolment in a specified educational program (12 hours
-- a month). Not indexed (s 2.26 is not in s 2.13). The enrolment conditions of s 2.26(1)(b)(ii) are asked as facts.
GIVEN `months enrolled full-time` IS A NUMBER, `other months enrolled part-time` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the education credit under s 2.26` `months enrolled full-time` `other months enrolled part-time` MEANS
    `the appropriate percentage` TIMES ((400 TIMES `months enrolled full-time`) PLUS (120 TIMES `other months enrolled part-time`))

§§ `s 2.32 -- the deduction for taxable dividends`

-- s 2.32: for an individual resident on the last day of the year, "(a) 6% of the total amount required under paragraph
-- 82(1)(a) and subparagraph 82(1)(b)(i) of the federal Act to be included in computing the individual's income" (dividends
-- other than eligible dividends, with their gross-up) and "(b) 11.5% of the total amount required under paragraph
-- 82(1)(a.1) and subparagraph 82(1)(b)(ii)" (eligible dividends, with their gross-up).
GIVEN `resident on the last day of the year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `taxable amount of dividends other than eligible dividends` IS A NUMBER
      `taxable amount of eligible dividends` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the dividend deduction under s 2.32` `resident on the last day of the year` `taxable amount of dividends other than eligible dividends` `taxable amount of eligible dividends` MEANS
    IF `resident on the last day of the year`
    THEN (6% TIMES `taxable amount of dividends other than eligible dividends`) PLUS (11.5% TIMES `taxable amount of eligible dividends`)
    ELSE 0

§§ `The tax payable`

-- The credits and the dividend deduction "may be deducted" in computing the tax payable under the Part; the encoding does
-- not let them take the tax below nil (NOTES.md finding 4). The s 2.12 and s 2.43 additions are not encoded.
GIVEN `tax under s 2.11(4)` IS A NUMBER, `total credits and deductions` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the tax payable after credits` `tax under s 2.11(4)` `total credits and deductions` MEANS
    `nil if negative` (`tax under s 2.11(4)` MINUS `total credits and deductions`)

-- Whether the encoding can answer for this person and year.
GIVEN `resident on the last day of the year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `had income earned outside the Northwest Territories` IS A BOOLEAN
      `tax year` IS A NUMBER
      `amount taxable` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE `Why not covered`
`why the tax is not covered` `resident on the last day of the year` `had income earned outside the Northwest Territories` `tax year` `amount taxable` MEANS
    IF NOT `resident on the last day of the year`
    THEN JUST `only an individual resident in the Northwest Territories on the last day of the year is encoded (s 2(1)(a)); s 2(1)(b) is not`
    ELSE IF `had income earned outside the Northwest Territories`
         THEN JUST `income earned outside the Northwest Territories brings in the apportionment of s 2.44, which is not encoded`
         ELSE IF `tax year` LESS THAN 2005
              THEN JUST `only the 2005 and later taxation years are encoded (s 2.11(2))`
              ELSE IF `amount taxable` LESS THAN 0
                   THEN JUST `the amount taxable cannot be negative`
                   ELSE NOTHING

§ `NWT Child Benefit -- ss 3.1 to 3.4 and Income Tax Regulations s 1.1`

§§ `s 3.1 -- eligible individual and qualified dependant`

-- s 3.1(1) "eligible individual" in respect of a qualified dependant: (a) resides with the dependant, (b) is resident in
-- the Northwest Territories, (c) is the parent who primarily fulfils the responsibility for the care and upbringing, or a
-- shared custody parent, (d) is not described in federal s 149(1)(a) or (b) (officers and servants of another country and
-- their families), and (e) is, or whose cohabiting spouse or common-law partner is, a Canadian citizen, permanent
-- resident, protected person, member of a humanitarian designated class, or a temporary resident resident in Canada
-- throughout the preceding 18 months. "Primarily fulfils the responsibility" is a judgment made under the federal factors
-- (s 3.1(1)(f) to (h)): asked as a fact.
DECLARE `Care of the child` IS ONE OF
    `I am the parent who primarily fulfils the responsibility for the child's care and upbringing`
    `I am a shared custody parent`
    `neither`

GIVEN `I reside with the child` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am resident in the Northwest Territories` IS A BOOLEAN
      `care` IS A `Care of the child`
      `I am described in federal s 149(1)(a) or (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I or my cohabiting spouse meet the status test of paragraph (e)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an eligible individual under s 3.1` IF
        `I reside with the child`
    AND `I am resident in the Northwest Territories`
    AND (NOT (`care` EQUALS `neither`))
    AND (NOT `I am described in federal s 149(1)(a) or (b)`)
    AND `I or my cohabiting spouse meet the status test of paragraph (e)`

-- s 3.1(1) "qualified dependant": (a) under 18, (b) resides with an eligible individual in the Territories, (c) not a
-- person for whom the spouse amount was claimed federally by the person's own cohabiting spouse, (d) not a person for whom
-- a special allowance under the Children's Special Allowances Act is payable.
GIVEN `age` IS A NUMBER
      `resides with the eligible individual in the Territories` IS A BOOLEAN
      `claimed as a spouse by their own cohabiting spouse` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a children's special allowance is payable for them` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a qualified dependant under s 3.1` IF
        `age` LESS THAN 18
    AND `resides with the eligible individual in the Territories`
    AND (NOT `claimed as a spouse by their own cohabiting spouse`)
    AND (NOT `a children's special allowance is payable for them`)

§§ `s 3.2(1) -- when the overpayment is deemed made`

-- s 3.2(1): the person "and, where the Commissioner so demands, the person's cohabiting spouse or common-law partner ...
-- have filed a return of income for the year" (the base taxation year), and "(b) the person was resident in the Northwest
-- Territories at the beginning of the month and on the day before the month". s 3.3(1): the person is an eligible
-- individual for a month only if a notice in prescribed form was filed "no later than 11 months after the end of the
-- month" (or later if the Minister extends the time, s 3.3(2)).
GIVEN `I filed my return for the base taxation year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my spouse filed, if the Commissioner demanded it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `resident at the beginning of the month and on the day before` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I filed the notice in time or the Minister extended the time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the conditions of s 3.2(1) and s 3.3(1) are met` IF
        `I filed my return for the base taxation year`
    AND `my spouse filed, if the Commissioner demanded it`
    AND `resident at the beginning of the month and on the day before`
    AND `I filed the notice in time or the Minister extended the time`

-- s 3.1(1) "base taxation year": for January to June, the year that ended on 31 December of the second preceding calendar
-- year; for July to December, the year that ended on 31 December of the preceding calendar year.
GIVEN `month` IS A NUMBER, `calendar year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the base taxation year` `month` `calendar year` MEANS
    IF `month` AT MOST 6 THEN `calendar year` MINUS 2 ELSE `calendar year` MINUS 1

§§ `s 3.2(2) and Regulations s 1.1 -- the amount`

-- Regulations s 1.1(1)(b): C, "only if the person ... has qualified dependants who did not reach six years of age at the
-- beginning of the month": $815 for one, $1,467 for two, $1,997 for three, $2,445 for four, "$2,445 plus an additional
-- $367 for each of the fifth and subsequent".
GIVEN `number` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`prescribed amount C` `number` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `number` AT MOST 0 THEN 0
           IF `number` EQUALS 1 THEN 815
           IF `number` EQUALS 2 THEN 1467
           IF `number` EQUALS 3 THEN 1997
           OTHERWISE 2445 PLUS (367 TIMES (`number` MINUS 4))

-- Regulations s 1.1(1)(c): D, for "qualified dependants who are not described in paragraph (b)" (six or over): $652, $1,174,
-- $1,597, $1,956, "$1,956 plus an additional $293 for each of the fifth and subsequent".
GIVEN `number` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`prescribed amount D` `number` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `number` AT MOST 0 THEN 0
           IF `number` EQUALS 1 THEN 652
           IF `number` EQUALS 2 THEN 1174
           IF `number` EQUALS 3 THEN 1597
           OTHERWISE 1956 PLUS (293 TIMES (`number` MINUS 4))

-- Regulations s 1.1(1)(a), (d): B, the prescribed minimum threshold, $30,000; E, the prescribed maximum threshold, $80,000.
`prescribed minimum threshold B` MEANS 30000
`prescribed maximum threshold E` MEANS 80000

-- s 3.2(2): "If A is less than or equal to B, then (1/12)(C + D). If A is greater than B, then
-- (1/12)[C + D - (A - B)(C + D)/(E - B)]", A the eligible individual's adjusted income (federal s 122.6). Above E the
-- formula is negative; the encoding reads it as nil (NOTES.md finding 6).
GIVEN `adjusted income` IS A NUMBER
      `qualified dependants under six` IS A NUMBER
      `qualified dependants six or over` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the monthly overpayment under s 3.2(2)` `adjusted income` `qualified dependants under six` `qualified dependants six or over` MEANS
    IF `adjusted income` AT MOST `prescribed minimum threshold B`
    THEN cd DIVIDED BY 12
    ELSE `nil if negative` ((cd MINUS (((`adjusted income` MINUS `prescribed minimum threshold B`) TIMES cd) DIVIDED BY (`prescribed maximum threshold E` MINUS `prescribed minimum threshold B`))) DIVIDED BY 12)
    WHERE
        cd MEANS (`prescribed amount C` `qualified dependants under six`) PLUS (`prescribed amount D` `qualified dependants six or over`)

-- s 3.2(2.1): a shared custody parent gets (A + B)/2, A the s 3.2(2) amount and B that amount "calculated without
-- reference to ... subparagraph (c)(ii) of the definition eligible individual". Without (c)(ii) a shared custody parent
-- is not an eligible individual, so B is nil and the parent gets half (NOTES.md finding 7).
GIVEN `full monthly amount` IS A NUMBER, `care` IS A `Care of the child`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the monthly NWT Child Benefit for my care arrangement` `full monthly amount` `care` MEANS
    CONSIDER `care`
    WHEN `I am the parent who primarily fulfils the responsibility for the child's care and upbringing` THEN `full monthly amount`
    WHEN `I am a shared custody parent` THEN (`full monthly amount` PLUS 0) DIVIDED BY 2
    WHEN `neither` THEN 0

§ `Cost of Living Offset -- s 3.5 and Income Tax Regulations s 1.2`

-- Regulations s 1.2(1): Zones 1, 2 and 3 by community (listed in the regulation).
DECLARE `Offset zone` IS ONE OF `Zone 1`, `Zone 2`, `Zone 3`

-- Regulations s 1.2(2) (R-022-2023, R-022-2024, R-038-2025): in every zone A, B and C are "$0".
GIVEN `zone` IS AN `Offset zone`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`prescribed amount A for the offset` `zone` MEANS
    CONSIDER `zone`
    WHEN `Zone 1` THEN 0
    WHEN `Zone 2` THEN 0
    WHEN `Zone 3` THEN 0

GIVEN `zone` IS AN `Offset zone`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`prescribed amount B for the offset` `zone` MEANS
    CONSIDER `zone`
    WHEN `Zone 1` THEN 0
    WHEN `Zone 2` THEN 0
    WHEN `Zone 3` THEN 0

GIVEN `zone` IS AN `Offset zone`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`prescribed amount C for the offset` `zone` MEANS
    CONSIDER `zone`
    WHEN `Zone 1` THEN 0
    WHEN `Zone 2` THEN 0
    WHEN `Zone 3` THEN 0

-- s 3.5(1) "eligible individual": (a) 18 or over before the specified month, or at some earlier time a parent who resided
-- with the child or married or in a common-law partnership; and (b) resident in the Territories on the first day of the
-- specified month and of the preceding specified month. s 3.5(3): the individual must also file a return for the year.
GIVEN `18 or over, or was a parent living with the child, or married or in a common-law partnership` IS A BOOLEAN
      `resident on the first day of this and the preceding specified month` IS A BOOLEAN
      `filed a return of income for the year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is entitled to the offset under s 3.5(3)` IF
        `18 or over, or was a parent living with the child, or married or in a common-law partnership`
    AND `resident on the first day of this and the preceding specified month`
    AND `filed a return of income for the year`

-- s 3.5(3): the eligible individual "is deemed to have paid during the specified month, on account of the eligible
-- individual's tax payable ... an amount equal to 25% of ... A + B + C", B if the individual has a qualified relation and
-- C for each qualified dependant.
GIVEN `zone` IS AN `Offset zone`
      `has a qualified relation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `number of qualified dependants` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the offset deemed paid in a specified month` `zone` `has a qualified relation` `number of qualified dependants` MEANS
    25% TIMES (`prescribed amount A for the offset` `zone`
               PLUS (IF `has a qualified relation` THEN `prescribed amount B for the offset` `zone` ELSE 0)
               PLUS (`number of qualified dependants` TIMES `prescribed amount C for the offset` `zone`))
